# 0112 serves the anchor's GL capability limits the serving table never named
# and the clamp direction discarded, and stops --fingerprint-explain claiming
# they were served when they were not. It touches five files.
#
# ui/gl/gl_gl_api_implementation.cc carries most of it, and that file's own
# history is the ordering: 0026 created kApostateGlLimits and the
# glGetIntegerv hook, 0032 extended the table, 0035 and 0036 added the 64-bit
# and float query paths it also edits, and 0103 introduced
# BackendEnforcesGlLimits(), whose test this corrects and whose three call
# sites it rewrites. 0103 is the binding constraint there. It also reads the
# driver's unsubstituted GL_RENDERER through GLApiBase, which 0007 established
# as the substitution point, so 0007 comes ahead of it too.
#
# ui/gl/gl_gl_api_implementation.h is touched for the same reason: the three
# robust ANGLE query variants have to be declared as overrides before they
# can be defined, and those are what GLES2DecoderPassthroughImpl, the default
# decoder, actually calls. No other patch in the series touches that header,
# so it orders nothing.
#
# base/apostate/compose.cc carries the explain change: it rewrites the
# cross-backend limitation text 0102 wrote, and counts gl_limits on the
# profile merged by the anchor block 0081 wrote, so both come ahead of it.
# 0111 is the most recent patch to touch that file, so 0112 sits after it --
# not because it depends on 0111, but because its context must be the text
# 0111 left behind. It does not touch ComposeProfileForCurrentProcess, where
# 0113 works, and its compose.cc hunks are ~580 lines above 0113's earliest
# context line.
#
# base/apostate/profile.cc carries the loader fix: the gl_limits parse 0070
# wrote refuses any value that is not greater than zero, which silently drops
# the two measured limits that are not -- MIN_PROGRAM_TEXEL_OFFSET at -8 and
# MAX_SERVER_WAIT_TIMEOUT at 0. 0070 therefore comes ahead of it, and 0110 is
# the most recent patch to touch that file, so 0112 must follow 0110 too --
# for context, not for behaviour. Without this hunk the other two files are
# still wrong for those two limits, because they never reach gl_limits().
#
# base/apostate/profile.h gains the companion map for the few limits a device
# reports with a genuine fraction, so gl_limits() stays integral. Its only
# ordering constraint is that 0070 widened that storage to int64 first.
#
# It is inert on its own: five of the thirteen limits it serves are emitted
# only after the anchor_gl_layer filter fix in
# scripts/generate-dispersion-tables.py, which is not a patch and needs a
# rebuild rather than a series position.
0112-gl-serve-the-anchor-capability-limits.patch

