# It comes after 0081, which wrote base/apostate/compose.{h,cc},
# base/apostate/profile.{h,cc} and base/apostate/explain.{h,cc} -- every file
# it touches -- and after 0084, whose PreSandboxStartup call site is the point
# it relies on and does not change.
#
# After 0111 twice over, and this is the load-bearing one. 0111 made
# --fingerprint-locale the only thing that writes locale.accept_languages into
# a composed profile, which is why reading the switch here is complete rather
# than a shortcut; and 0111 wrote the resolve_locale() lambda, the
# LocaleInheritanceNote helper and the two "(inherited)" assertions in
# compose_unittest.cc that this patch rewrites. Its compose.cc hunks carry
# 0111's exact lines as context in both places.
#
# After 0106, which wrote the PayloadDescribesDevice branch and
# ReportAuthoredProfileBypass that its compose.cc hunks edit, and after 0110,
# which wrote profile.h's static payload-helper family that
# AcceptLanguagesInPayload joins and the profile.cc block it is appended after.
#
# After 0113, which is the last patch to touch the explain report and the
# compose_unittest.cc tail this appends past. It is independent of 0112.
0114-composed-locale-never-the-host-shell.patch

# 0115 makes the composed locale decide the application locale on macOS and
# Windows too. 0114 pinned the process environment, which is the linux lever
# and only the linux lever: macOS resolves from NSBundle's
# preferredLocalizations and Windows from the preferred-UI-language list, and
# neither reads the environment. On macOS that was not waiting for a build --
# the artifact ships Chromium.app wholesale and its framework has carried all
# 220 locale.pak files all along, so a composed persona has been serving its
# host's system language, measured, with navigator.languages disagreeing.
#
# It resolves the composed value in l10n_util::GetApplicationLocaleInternal,
# ahead of every platform candidate, which is one point instead of three
# platform slots -- and the only one above windows' pref_locale, where a
# kApplicationLocale stored in an existing --user-data-dir would otherwise
# outrank a composed persona through a persisted channel.
#
# It comes after 0114 and depends on it three ways. It adds
# ComposedApplicationLocale() beside the locale block 0114 wrote in
# base/apostate/compose.{h,cc}; it rewrites both of the
# InstallComposedLocaleEnvironment call sites 0114 left in
# InstallComposedProfile so that they read that accessor instead of computing
# the answer inline, which is what keeps the two pins from disagreeing; and its
# compose_unittest.cc hunk appends after the locale section 0114 added. It also
# needs 0114's environment write on macOS specifically: macOS is POSIX, so
# content adopted the operator's locale into the C library, and pinning only
# the resolution would leave the C library disagreeing with ICU -- the split
# ledger row intl.resolved-locale warns against.
#
# After 0111, whose resolve_locale() lambda it extends with the --lang
# limitation, and whose ComposeRequest::accept_languages -- recorded there as
# dead -- is what that limitation finally reads.
#
# It is the first patch in the series to touch ui/base/l10n, so nothing else
# orders it there. Independent of 0112 and 0113.
0115-composed-locale-outranks-the-platform.patch


